# Declared substitutions for measurements the host project expresses its own way.
#
# FORMAT   key<TAB>the literal this project uses instead
#
# A project with its own scale will not contain the literals in layout.txt. Tailwind
# writes w-62 or w-[248px]; Chakra writes space.4; a design-token pipeline writes
# --size-sidebar. All of those are correct - the ratios survive, the values bend to the
# host - and all of them would fail a check that only looks for "248px".
#
# So declare the substitution. The checker then requires YOUR literal instead:
#
#     sidebar.width	w-[248px]
#     space.4	p-4
#     radius.card	rounded-xl
#
# WHY DECLARE IT AT ALL, rather than skipping the check? Because a declared substitution
# can be read by a person in ten seconds, and a silent one cannot be read at all. This
# file is the difference between "we used the project's scale" and "we did not check".
# It is also the machine-readable half of the rule that /setup must report every
# substitution it made.
#
# A substitution that maps a value to something that is NOT equivalent is not caught
# here - nothing can check that w-62 is 248px. It is caught by a reviewer reading this
# file, which is exactly why the file is short and exactly why it must not be padded
# with entries nobody intends to read.
#
# This build uses the values as written, so there is nothing to declare.
